ref_dict.rem:exact degree:
\begin{rem}\label{rem:exact degree}
    A critical point to note is that this is the only part of the entire proof that utilises the exact bound $\delta^*(G) \ge n - \floor{\frac{n}{t}} - (k - 3)$ via \cref{obs:min 1-degree,lem:disjoint edges cherries}. As mentioned in \Cref{sec:intro}, we can prove \cref{thm:Hamilton cycle extremal} and consequently \cref{thm:main} with the weaker bound of $\delta^*(G) \ge n - \floor{\frac{n}{t}} - (k - 2)$ instead, for most values of $k$ and $\ell$ (namely when $t \ge \ell+2$ or when $\ell = k-1$) which is achieved by modifying \cref{lem:disjoint edges cherries} to potentially allow for an additional cherry or some edges. We discuss how to suitably adapt the rest of the proof in \Cref{sec:improving the bound}.
\end{rem}

